    "question": {
      ":question/id": "769da764-b646-560a-b21e-f26d2daaa831",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-3 & =8x-3 \\\\ 8x-3-8x & =8x-3-8x \\\\ -3 & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & =4x+8 \\\\ 4x+2-4x & =4x+8-4x \\\\ 2 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $4x+2=4x+8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+9 & =-5x-1 \\\\ x+9+5x-9 & =-5x-1+5x-9 \\\\ 6x & =-10 \\\\ x & =- \\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $x+9=-5x-1$ has the unique solution $x=- \\frac{5}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $4x+2=4x+8$ only.",
