      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y+9 & =-4y-9 \\\\ -3y+9+4y-9 & =-4y-9+4y-9 \\\\ y & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-3y+9=-4y-9$ has the unique solution $y=-18.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y+4 & =5y-7 \\\\ 5y+4-5y & =5y-7-5y \\\\ 4 & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $5y+4=5y-7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6y-5 & =-6y-5 \\\\ -6y-5+6y & =-6y-5+6y \\\\ -5 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $5y+4=5y-7$ only.",
