      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+6 & =x-3 \\\\ x+6-x & =x-3-x \\\\ 6 & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $x+6=x-3$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+7 & =-4x+7 \\\\ -3x+7+4x-7 & =-4x+7+4x-7 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-3x+7=-4x+7$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-2 & =8x-9 \\\\ 8x-2-8x & =8x-9-8x \\\\ -2 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $8x-2=8x-9$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x+6=x-3$; $8x-2=8x-9$ only.",
