    "question": {
      ":question/id": "08f24ae2-ed05-5dc0-8724-b38082362fbe",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6w-4 & =6w-6 \\\\ 6w-4-6w & =6w-6-6w \\\\ -4 & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $6w-4=6w-6$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w-7 & =3w-7 \\\\ 3w-7-3w & =3w-7-3w \\\\ -7 & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7w-1 & =-8w+1 \\\\ -7w-1+8w+1 & =-8w+1+8w+1 \\\\ w & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-7w-1=-8w+1$ has the unique solution $w=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $6w-4=6w-6$ only.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "193f7b40-678f-52b0-87f5-fd6d487ab20f",
